---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Wayline from '../components/Wayline.astro';
---

<Layout title="Podcast — Don't Lose Your Way" description="Documentary-style stories for those who carry weight no one sees. Sometimes it helps to hear a voice that knows.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h1>Podcast</h1>
      <p>Documentary-style stories for those who carry weight no one sees. Sometimes it helps to hear a voice that knows.</p>

      <h2>The Don't Lose Your Way Podcast</h2>
      <p class="working-title">A working title — the show's final name is still being chosen.</p>
      <p>This is where the podcast is going: one voice — Carlos, telling his own story. Each episode opens with the same introduction, walks through one chapter of what he went through, and closes with what he is building toward next. New episodes will appear here as they are ready.</p>

      <Wayline />

      <h2>Start Here</h2>

      <h3>One More Minute</h3>
      <p>Survival Mental Health Silence</p>
      <p>If you only listen to one episode first, begin here. This story is about the pause between pain and decision — and how one more minute can change everything.</p>
      <p>
        <audio controls preload="none" src="https://dontloseyourway.com/audio/podcast/one-more-minute.mp3">
          Your browser does not support the audio element. <a href="https://dontloseyourway.com/audio/podcast/one-more-minute.mp3">Download the episode</a>.
        </audio>
      </p>

      <h2>Take a Minute</h2>
      <p>What are you feeling right now?</p>
      <p>What is something you have survived that people may not see?</p>
      <p>Who could you reach out to today, even if it is just one person?</p>
      <p>You do not need to answer everything today. Start with one honest moment.</p>

      <h2>Season One: Before It Breaks</h2>
      <p>The first season explores the moments before everything changes — the silence, the anger, the loneliness, and the decisions that shape whether someone keeps going.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Episode 1 — One More Minute</strong> (above)</li>
        <li>Episode 2 — I Almost Did It · Planned</li>
        <li>Episode 3 — Anger Has a Voice · Planned</li>
        <li>Episode 4 — Nobody Saw Me Heal · Planned</li>
        <li>Episode 5 — Choose Yourself · Planned</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Send a Voice Message</h2>
      <p>Some future episodes may include anonymous voice messages from listeners who want to share a story, reflection, or moment they made it through.</p>
      <p>Voice submissions can be reviewed before being featured. Anonymous options will be available.</p>
      <p>If you are in immediate distress, call or text 988 (U.S.). This site is not a crisis service.</p>
      <p><strong>Phone:</strong> 988</p>
      <p>Written reflections are open now: <a href="/chapel">the Chapel</a> is a moderated, anonymous room where you can leave a few words tonight and read others who have stood where you stand.</p>

      <h2>The music</h2>
      <p>The <em>Healing Trauma Through AI Music</em> series grew out of this same place. <a href="https://soundcloud.com/carlos-cabrales-iii/sets/healing-trauma-through-ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Listen on SoundCloud →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    audio { width: 100%; max-width: 36rem; min-height: 44px; }
    .working-title { font-style: italic; }
    .wayline { margin: 2.5rem auto 0.5rem; }
  </style>
</Layout>
